Actually, I would like to use t-distribution in the regression model, adding the 'nu' parameter (degrees-of-freedom or normality parameter which controls mean (mu) and SD (sigma) from non-normal data). I don´t know how to use it in 'blavaan' scripts...

Example: mod<- 'Inteligence ~ Age + Education'
fit<-bsem(mod, data=data)

# JAGS t-distribution (using 1 or 2 groups):
  modelString = "
  model {
    for ( i in 1:Ntotal ) {
      y[i] ~ dt( mu[x[i]] , 1/sigma[x[i]]^2 , nu )
    }
    for ( j in 1:2 ) { # 2 groups
      mu[j] ~ dnorm( meanY , 1/(100*sdY)^2 )
      sigma[j] ~ dunif( sdY/1000 , sdY*1000 )
    }
    nu ~ dexp(1/30.0)
}

